  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The physicist John Brandenburg puts forward a theory that the craft said to have come down near Roswell in 1947 were flying low through a lightning storm, scanning the ground for plutonium. In his account they flew two craft close together, so that one could pick up the background noise while the other picked up the signal. He tells Michels this as his own reading and credits a book called Cosmic Awakening. On this theory, the crash would be the result of a survey of America's first nuclear material."
